Disagreements the differential test (tests/fuzz.sh, M20) found, minimised by hand. Each is a program eezott judges
otherwise than the oracle does; kept as found, never deleted, and promoted to tests/tt or tests/tt/bad once the
disagreement is resolved (a fix on our side, or a recorded difference between the theories). Blame our
implementation first: every entry below was ours.

type_in_type_1.tt      eezott ACCEPTS uu : U := K U with K {A : U} (x : A) : U := A. The implicit {A} is a meta whose
                       solution (U, in U 1) never constrains the level of its type; K is taken at level 0, so U : U.
                       With {A} written explicitly (type_in_type_explicit.tt) it is rightly refused: 'U 1 is not below U'.
type_in_type_2.tt      ... and self : uu := U is accepted: U : U inhabited (Type-in-Type through an implicit argument).
pinned_level_lifted.tt Cover : S1 -> U pins its hidden level to 0 (ua^0 against the motive U) yet stays polymorphic:
                       coverBig : S1 -> U 1 := Cover is accepted, an instance whose body is ill-typed at that level.
level_bisection.tt     b1/b2 (explicit {A}) take isPropNeg at the hidden level; b6 (inferred {A}) at 0: the bisection
                       that located the first defect, from the prelude's own stableEqIsSet failing in Agda.
boundary_image_right.tt  eezott REJECTS the CHM-correct swap method for QVec ('expected qcons (suc n) x (qcons n y ih)')
boundary_image_wrong.tt  and ACCEPTS the wrong one: E_con_spine images a constructor in a boundary with its recursive
                       arguments' images in the ELEMENT positions too (m_c E(a).. E(a_rec).., CHM: m_c a.. E(a_rec)..).
                       Masked in the suite because every HIT motive there ignores its element arguments.
